{
    "article_summary": "The article describes an electrochemical method for the selective hydrocarboxylation of acrylamides with CO2. By tuning the solvent and electrolyte, the authors achieved precise control over regioselectivity, enabling the synthesis of either \u03b1-carboxylation or \u03b2-carboxylation products. The reaction operates under mild conditions without the need for chemical reductants, utilizing a magnesium anode and graphite cathode.",
